 6. + This 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Mady again. We have to talk about AI-writing-gate, or legendary investor Stanley Druckenmiller admitting to using AI for his op-ed in the Wall Street Journal. 

 There are two schools of thought: those who view AI-ified writing as heinous, and those who think this is the future and anyone who questions it is rubbing two sticks together after matches were invented. The life lesson I hold closest to my heart is that the truth is always in the middle, but that won't stop people from fighting passionately about it on X. 
 
